### ----------------------
### Auth: OAuth
### ----------------------
### 1/2 Github OAuth: First authorize link
# Go to this URL manually and copy the `code` value on redirect
GET https://github.com/login/oauth/authorize?client_id={{github.oauth.client-id}}&scope=repo

### Github OAuth
# 2/2 Put the code value here and submit
POST https://github.com/login/oauth/access_token?code=223e0cc11bd75c1ed129&client_id={{github.oauth.client-id}}&
    client_secret={{github.oauth.client-secret}}

### ----------------------
### Auth: App - install app
### ----------------------
# 1/3 Prepare request to get an access token: https://docs.github.com/en/apps/creating-github-apps/authenticating-with-a-github-app/generating-a-json-web-token-jwt-for-a-github-app
# 2. Send request for an access token in below query
# 2. Use that token as the Authorization: Bearer <value>
#
# To generate a token you need a JWT. Go to https://jwt.io/
#
# Under header, change "typ" to "RS256".
#
# Use this format for the payload:
#{
#  "iat": 1746492759,
#  "exp": 1746492999,
#  "iss": "Iv23li6VlSwmVqY3Zsjs"
#}
# For the PEM on jwt.io, the contents can be found in secrets (attached .pem file). This is NOT the secret for the Github App.
#
# To get the times for the payload:
# 1. Copy the big, incrementing number at: https://www.unixtimestamp.com/
# 2. Paste that as "iat" (time will elapse while doing these steps so it will be in the past)
# 3. Paste it as "exp" but increment by less than 600 (10 minutes)
#
# Then submit the request to ../access_tokens.

### 2/3: Github app: Request access token
# Bearer = JST from above
POST https://api.github.com/app/installations/65862682/access_tokens
Accept: application/vnd.github+json
